b9=A.a([A.w(h8,'A "safe tile" is one unlikely to help opponents win. The safest tiles are ones already discarded by the player you\'re worried about - BUT only within the SAME turn-rotation!',h9,h9),A.w(h8,"Why? If they threw {{east}} this rotation, they can't need {{east}} for a Pong right now. That tile is absolutely safe against them - until they draw again!",h9,h9),A.w(h8,"Once an opponent draws a new tile, their previous discard is no longer guaranteed safe. It becomes only RELATIVELY safe - they might have picked up a tile that now pairs with it. Re-assess every rotation!",h9,h9),A.w(h8,"Other safe tiles: tiles that multiple opponents have discarded, tiles where all 4 copies are visible, and tiles adjacent to their discards. Dangerous tiles: fresh tiles (never seen before), middle tiles (4,5,6) in late game.",h9,h9)],n5)
